---
description: Guardrails for the NSE pairs trading refactor
alwaysApply: true
---

- This is a refactor, not a rewrite. Preserve exact numeric behavior from the
  original monolith script unless explicitly told otherwise.
- Never change a random_state, threshold constant, or statistical formula
  without flagging it clearly in your response first and waiting for confirmation.
- Files stats.py, features.py, and backtest.py contain financial logic where
  subtle bugs (lookahead bias, off-by-one shifts, sign errors) are invisible
  in normal testing. When editing these files, explain what changed and why,
  even for small edits.
- Prefer small, single-module diffs over large multi-file rewrites.
- Every new function that touches price data or model predictions should have
  a corresponding test in tests/.
- Do not add new dependencies without asking first — this project has zero budget
  for paid APIs or services.